  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "Right now",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "For 'am / is / are doing', add **-ছ-** plus the person ending to the verb stem:\n\n- আমি **করছি** — I am doing\n- তুমি **করছো** — you are doing (familiar)\n- আপনি **করছেন** — you are doing (polite)\n- সে **করছে** — he/she is doing\n\nCompare the simple present: **আমি কাজ করি** 'I work' (in general) vs **আমি কাজ করছি** 'I am working' (right now).\n\nWith vowel stems the ছ doubles up as **চ্ছ**: খা- → **খাচ্ছি** 'I'm eating', যা- → **যাচ্ছি** 'I'm going'.\n\n**তুমি কী করছো?** 'What are you doing?' is a common phone opener. A natural answer: **রান্না করছি** 'I'm cooking' — the আমি can drop, because the ending already says who.",
